# L5R 5E - CHILDREN OF THE FIVE WINDS: ADVENTURE SEEDS (FRAME)
# Source: Children of the Five Winds.

FRAME "L5R5e_ChildrenOfFiveWinds_AdventureSeeds" {
    NAME "Children of the Five Winds — Adventure Seeds"
    VERSION "0.4.1"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.4"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-09-02"
    DEPENDS_ON "L5R5e_Core_Core"

    DESCRIPTION "Adventure seeds presented in sidebars throughout Children of the Five Winds, for GMs to expand into full adventures."

    ENTRIES {
        ENTRY ^"THE CURSED WOMAN" {
            TYPE "hook"
            TAGS ["children-of-five-winds"]
            DESCRIPTION "Hook: Hafsa bint Shadah appears to be under the effects of a dangerous curse! First, a heavy clay pot fell and narrowly missed her head. Then, a deadly serpent was found in her bedroom! Hafsa's daughter, Ulma, requests assistance in banishing the evil spirits or malicious djinn who are plaguing her mother, who refuses to believe in 'superstitious nonsense.' Rising Action: The so-called 'curse' is nothing of the kind. Rather, one of Hafsa's debtors is desperately trying to kill her before his loan is due. Nasu, an Ujik from a wealthy family, took out a large loan ostensibly to buy horses to trade in al-Zawira. Instead, he drank and gambled away most of the money in the Lucky Donkey. Now he is in debt not only to Hafsa but to the White Lady as well. When the PCs find him, Nasu attempts to hire them as bodyguards, with vague promises of future wealth and favors. Climax: Nasu gains an unexpected reprieve and a worrisome ally: the White Lady has her own reasons to want Hafsa dead and has offered to forgive Nasu's debt if he arranges the deed. Nasu steps up his attempts at murder by setting Hafsa's coffee house on fire, which may have dangerous repercussions for innocent bystanders or the PCs! Nasu's incompetence threatens the White Lady, so she sends her own much more competent killers to clean things up and leave Nasu as the fall guy. Any unfortunate witnesses (like the PCs) will have to be eliminated as well."
        }
        ENTRY ^"THE DARK HORSE" {
            TYPE "hook"
            TAGS ["children-of-five-winds"]
            DESCRIPTION "Hook: The Calamac ordu has recently come into possession of a superior black stallion, which it was able to buy very cheaply. But misfortune has followed after—Calamac Tygan was thrown and broke his leg, and another Calamac cousin, Gorgu, died mysteriously in the night, his broken body found behind his yurt. Fearing a curse, or worse, treachery from the Menghes family, the Calamacs may reach out to PCs with reputations as diplomats or investigators. Rising Action: Tracing the origin of the mysterious stallion reveals that it was, in fact, sold by the Menghes family to the Calamac family via an ignorant go-between. But Menghes Benve claims that the horse simply appeared in their herd one day and had been such a menace to any rider or even passerby that she had tried to get rid of it quickly. She knows nothing of any curse or any deaths. Meanwhile, signs of some animal attempting to gain access to the Calamac family shrine have been found all around the shrine's yurt, despite the mysterious horse being firmly locked away in a paddock all night. Climax: The horse is a spirit, either a reincarnation or an echo of Menghes Orojin. (Use the characteristics of a Wind Horse, page 156, with the Trickster template [see the core rulebook, page 311]; the horse can mask its supernatural nature easily, especially during the day.) Angry at both the Menghes and Calamac families, the Orojin-horse is attempting to gain access to the swords it bore in life, stored in the Calamac shrine. It will kill to do so and take its revenge on those who fought alongside Orojin and allowed him to die in battle with barbarians. There is only one person in the ordu whom the horse will neither trouble nor disobey: Orojin's former betrothed, Calamac Alma. If the PCs do not intervene, the horse-spirit will eventually cause such chaos that Alma will enter the temple (which the horse-spirit cannot do) and bring out the swords, at which point the horse will steal the swords and ride off into the Spirit Realms, never to be seen again."
        }
    }
}
